<title>BRAZIL: TENNIS-WASHINGTON PULLS OUT OF DAVIS CUP RUBBER.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-WASHINGTON PULLS OUT OF DAVIS CUP RUBBER.</headline>
<dateline>RIBEIRAO PRETO, Brazil 1997-02-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malivai Washington of the United States has pulled out of Sunday's Davis Cup reverse singles against Brazil's Fernando Meligeni, team sources said.</p>
<p>Washington, who has an injury to his left knee, will be replaced by Alex O'Brien.</p>
<p>The United States go into the final day of the world group, first round tie with a 2-1 lead. Jim Courier plays Gustavo Kuerten in the first reverse singles.</p>
